== Public Holidays in Japan == The current Japanese legal framework for "holidays" is governed by several laws, including: - The Act on National Holidays, enacted in [[:en:1948|1948]]. - The Act on Holidays of Agencies of the Diet. - The Act on Holidays of Courts (see: [[s:裁判所の休日に関する法律]]). - The Act on Holidays of Administrative Agencies.{{Refnest|[https://laws.e-gov.go.jp/law/363AC0000000091 Act on Holidays of Administrative Agencies] - [[e-gov.go.jp]]}}
A separate section covers Japanese local and national holidays in detail.
